{
  "schema_version": "1.9.2",
  "id": "USN-9119-1",
  "summary": "pdfresurrect vulnerabilities",
  "details": "It was discovered that PDFResurrect did not properly validate certain size\nvalues when loading PDF pages. If a user or automated system were tricked\ninto opening a specially crafted PDF file, an attacker could possibly use\nthis issue to cause PDFResurrect to crash, resulting in a denial of\nservice, or possibly execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2019-14934)\n\nIt was discovered that PDFResurrect did not properly validate the header of\nPDF files, leading to a heap buffer overflow. If a user or automated system\nwere tricked into opening a specially crafted PDF file, an attacker could\npossibly use this issue to cause PDFResurrect to crash, resulting in a\ndenial of service, or possibly execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2020-20740)",
